    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nSince 3.1 (#6652), `libcpp/string.pxd` cimports `libcpp.string_view`. As a result, any module that cimports `libcpp.string` gets `#include <string_view>` in its generated code, even if it never uses `string_view`. This breaks compilation with C++ standard libraries that don't provide the C++17 `<string_view>` header.\n\n\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n```cython\n# distutils: language = c++\nfrom libcpp.string cimport string\n\ndef f(string s):\n    return s\n```\nThe same code compiles with Cython 3.0.x. This is similar to #6896, where the C++11 `<type_traits>` header was included regardless of the C++ version.\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nModules that only use `std::string` compile without a C++17 standard library.\n\n### OS\n\nSolaris 11 (SPARC)\n\n### Python version\n\n3.8\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.2.9 (also present on master)\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
    "closed_at": null,
